{"name":"Flower of Oahu","hex":"#f5dfc5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"},{"title":"Oʻahu","blocks":[{"text":"Oʻahu, sometimes written Oahu, is the third-largest and most populated island of the Hawaiian Islands and of the U.S. state of Hawaii. The state capital, Honolulu, is on Oʻahu's southeastern coast. The island of Oʻahu and the uninhabited Northwestern Hawaiian Islands constitute the City and County of Honolulu. In 2025, Oʻahu had a population of 988,703, a decline of 27,791 from 1,016,494 in 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Oahu.jpg/330px-Oahu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/O%CA%BBahu"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/500px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/1280px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/500px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhalaenopsis_bellina_(Blue_Pink_x_sib)_(Rchb.f.)_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_(1995)._20210623_013709.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG/500px-Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG/1280px-Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG/500px-Sunflower_from_Silesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam